# Six core primitives

I would make WorkerKit only six things initially.

### 1. Work Ledger

This is absolutely necessary for the reason you gave.

The worker needs to remember:

```text
seen
considered
skipped
applied
claimed
working
submitted
rejected
accepted
paid
```

For every opportunity:

```json
{
  "fingerprint": "...",
  "platform": "moltjobs",
  "external_id": "...",
  "first_seen": "...",
  "last_seen": "...",
  "status": "submitted",
  "attempts": 1,
  "submission_id": "...",
  "worker_id": "...",
  "outcome": null
}
```

And `get-me-money` already has a good fingerprint mechanism based on platform + external ID/URL/title.

So:

```text
job discovered
      ↓
fingerprint
      ↓
Have I seen this?
 ├─ yes → update status/info
 └─ no  → evaluate
```

That immediately stops the maddening "agent discovers the same 50 gigs every morning" problem.

---

### 2. WorkRun Recorder

From the moment it chooses:

> **START WORK**

everything belongs to a WorkRun.

```text
run_0192
│
├── opportunity
├── task contract
├── initial plan
│
├── actions/
│   ├── searches
│   ├── pages
│   ├── tool calls
│   ├── repositories
│   └── decisions
│
├── skills/
│   ├── activated
│   ├── acquired
│   └── versions
│
├── work/
│
├── artifacts/
│
├── verification/
│
├── submission/
│
├── economics/
│
└── outcome/
```

Not all of that needs to be shoved into LLM memory.

Store the raw event stream.

Then **distill it afterward**.

```text
RAW RUN
   ↓
experience distiller
   ↓
"What actually mattered?"
   ↓
persistent worker memory
```

This is the scalable part.

