# 4. Core Worker Skillpack

And yes, **Moltwork itself should ship basic working skills**.

Not 100.

Maybe six.

```text
moltwork-core/
│
├── find-work/
├── evaluate-work/
├── compile-brief/
├── execute-professionally/
├── review-submission/
└── learn-from-outcome/
```

These are meta-professional skills.

## `find-work`

Knows:

* don't rediscover already-known jobs;
* query multiple sources;
* freshness;
* deadlines;
* pay;
* eligibility;
* competition;
* record everything.

## `evaluate-work`

Calculates:

```text
P(success)
reward
cost
competition
time
payment reliability
learning value
reusability
```

Your existing `Evaluation` model already has almost all of those fields.

## `compile-brief`

Transforms garbage marketplace prose into:

```text
objective
deliverables
acceptance criteria
constraints
deadline
submission mechanism
payment mechanism
```

## `execute-professionally`

Generic workflow:

```text
understand
→ research
→ acquire capabilities
→ plan
→ execute
→ self-check
→ artifact
```

## `review-submission`

Independent critic.

Your Executor already has a separate verifier before submission—which is exactly the right architecture.

## `learn-from-outcome`

After settlement/rejection:

```text
What worked?
What failed?
What should be remembered?
Was a reusable procedure discovered?
Does an existing skill need modification?
Should we propose a new skill?
```

Those six are basically the **curriculum for having a job**.

