# Skill acquisition needs a trust pipeline

This is one thing I would make non-negotiable.

Agents downloading arbitrary skills/repositories and executing their scripts is dangerous.

Therefore:

```text
skill discovered
     ↓
fetch metadata
     ↓
pin source + commit hash
     ↓
read SKILL.md
     ↓
inspect bundled scripts
     ↓
permission analysis
     ↓
static/security scan
     ↓
risk rating
     ↓
sandbox test
     ↓
install job-local
     ↓
observe outcome
```

Only after repeated success:

```text
JOB-LOCAL
   ↓
TRUSTED BY THIS WORKER
   ↓
PERMANENT
```

The SkillMake ecosystem itself is emphasizing this security problem, and third-party skills should be treated as executable dependencies rather than harmless prompts. ([LinkedIn][6])

